-- statement:
--   **The near-identity hypotheses give positive pivots.**
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegLn10`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.pivPos_of : ∀ (L : List ℕ) (A : ℕ → ℕ → ℤ)
--       (b : ℕ → ℤ) (η : ℝ), L.Nodup → 0 ≤ η → η + (L.length : ℝ) ^ 2 / 2 ^ P ≤ 1 / 2 →
--       (∀ i ∈ L, ∑ k ∈ L.toFinset, |(A i k : ℝ) / 2 ^ P - kd i k| ≤ η) →
--       (∀ i ∈ L, ∀ k ∈ L, ¬ S i k → A i k = 0) → PatOK S L → PivPos P S L A
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Segmented inverse (S2), machine side 10: the solver maps zero to zero
--
--   `B₀` must send an all-zero line to an all-zero line (the padded entries of the tensor stay
--   exactly zero). The only non-obvious step is the rounded division `fdiv P 0 d = 0`, true for
--   `d ≥ 0`: every pivot of the elimination is positive in the near-identity regime.
--
--   * `PivPos`, **`geSolveS_zero`**: nonnegative pivots give `geSolveS … 0 = 0`;
--   * **`pivPos_of`**: the hypotheses of `geSolveS_eq` give nonnegative pivots (same induction);
--   * **`segInvS_zero`** (hypotheses of `segInvS_eq`), **`segInvFullS_zero`** (parameter
--     hypotheses of `segInvFullS_err`).
